Seed: Split stops one step early on a discrete range: the last piece is taken when the next boundary reaches the range's last value rather than passing it
Oracles: RangeSplitOracleTests
Fails: every discrete range whose length is a multiple of the step plus one, on every discrete type: its last two pieces come out as one; and every calendar split whose last period ends one day before the range
History: planted before Split shipped in 10.0.0

